13
01:00:50,400 --> 01:00:56,400
24 Hour Party People is a 2002 British biographical comedy drama film about Manchester's
popular music community from 1976 to 1992, and specifically about Factory Records.

14
01:05:31,200 --> 01:05:37,200
It was written by Frank Cottrell Boyce and directed by Michael Winterbottom.

15
01:10:12,000 --> 01:10:18,000
The film was entered into the 2002 Cannes Film Festival to positive reviews.

16
01:14:52,800 --> 01:14:58,800
It begins with the punk rock era of the late 1970s and moves through the 1980s into the rave
and DJ culture and the "Madchester" scene of the late 1980s and early 1990s.

17
01:19:33,600 --> 01:19:39,600
The main character is Tony Wilson (played by Steve Coogan), a news
reporter for Granada Television and the head of Factory Records.

18
01:24:14,400 --> 01:24:20,400
The narrative largely follows his career, while also covering the careers of the major Factory artists,
especially Joy Division and New Order, A Certain Ratio, the Durutti Column and Happy Mondays.

19
01:28:55,199 --> 01:29:01,199
The film is a dramatisation based on a combination of real events, rumours, urban
legends and the imaginings of the scriptwriter, as the film makes clear.

20
01:33:36,000 --> 01:33:42,000
In one scene, one-time Buzzcocks member Howard Devoto (played by Martin Hancock) is shown having sex with Wilson's first wife in the toilets
of a club; the real Devoto, an extra in the scene, turns to the camera and says, "I definitely don't remember this happening".

21
01:38:16,800 --> 01:38:22,800
The fourth wall is frequently broken, with Wilson (who also acts as the narrator) frequently commenting on events directly
to camera as they occur, at one point declaring that he is "being postmodern, before it's fashionable".

22
01:42:57,600 --> 01:43:03,600
The actors are often intercut with real contemporary concert footage, including the
Sex Pistols' June and July 1976 gig at the Lesser Free Trade Hall.

23
01:47:38,400 --> 01:47:44,400
The film explores themes of northern england, based on
novel or book, 1970s, nightclub, clubbing.

24
01:52:19,200 --> 01:52:25,200
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
